  "authoringNote": "Migrated from F01; expectations re-derived under pack v2. Scope is explicit and supported, the named supplier record f01-supplier-status v1 is current, usable and matches the case, and the order states K0823, so R01 passes and cites the seven supplier fields and the order code. Every subject-scoped version matches the case subject in metadata and states the exact case name and identifier, so R02 passes and cites the six beneficiary facts. The one current usable order states every element (R03 pass, nine citations). Final encounter 2026-08-20 and final order 2026-09-02 share SYN-PRAC-0001, and the order follows the encounter within the 2027-02-20 bound (R04 pass, C01; six citations: status, date and practitioner identifier of each; no time is stated, so no timestamp is cited). The receipt references f01-order v1 and states 2026-09-03T17:05:00Z, after the C06 span of the order date (2026-09-01T10:00Z to 2026-09-03T12:00Z), so R05 passes with four citations. R06 is the case-level qualified clinical review condition citing the five clinical statements, with no administrative effect. No LCMP incorporation is stated (R07 pass, citing the false flag; the null evaluation date is not cited). The pack is reviewed and 2026-10-18 is supported (R08); every hash matches and every body parses exactly (R09). R10 is not applicable to a pure assessment. No condition holds outside R06 and R10, every parent document set is empty, and the state is ready_for_review. v1 differences: pack and schema pins only; R06 and R10 now carry their condition tuples.",
